    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1280">

                <pb facs="1239" n="1073" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg1073"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.115R39/19</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Fletcher to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-12T15:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 12, 1917, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>85. My telegram No. 81, April 11, 3 p.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1280-f1"/> I am
                    informed that the Sonora authorities have been ordered by telegraph to suspend
                    proceedings as requested and to make a report on the matter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fletcher</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
